{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1efa3524b52f3987b44568202341fb57f9bcc4690f043de7b8cefcdb6ad1a2a4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Hands-on examples require a development environment with Node.js and a simple Next.js setup, plus access to Claude Code with appropriate authentication and pricing configuration."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3a837e59a0a02f7039969271bd8c31d0eef2232f07e867cba4304b03a513b78e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"This repository is the companion code repository for the Packt book 'Agentic Coding with Claude Code, First Edition' by Eden Marco."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3c667a14832daaa246808d3322d6c555f1f29f6ac9849d33169686cf98d84643"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The book teaches designing multi-agent systems using subagents, parallel sessions, and hierarchical delegation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_58f61a5716b19a1cbaf02417f0dcb8862b576f7129b139aeaa90c9348cee7710"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Among the book's stated key learnings are building reusable slash commands and hooks, creating persistent AI memory with memory files, and enforcing coding standards through project documentation and context control."},{"claim_ids":["clm_774edcad2b1ed0593af3dcd5ce780b6ae055a3ff4f1e1640ef3098ae236838e0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The book covers the Model Context Protocol, including its motivation, core architecture, and configuring MCP servers inside Claude Code, and discusses trade-offs between MCP, skills, and subagents."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9d356b9b31b18c64cafdfdc905df00ca6882c22ad6f999a655f9d75793dbda82"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The book assumes prior software development experience, Python or TypeScript proficiency, basic Git knowledge, and familiarity with LLM concepts such as agents, RAG, and ReAct; it does not cover beginner-level programming or introductory generative AI topics."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bf3223ed98b30224c316967a0253b04e660594afe9cdf786952b2b8e3c59c411"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The book covers controlling Claude Code via slash commands, persistent memory files, and lifecycle hooks for automating development tasks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fa977be76ec5f0fc2072538600fb0c53c104162583bd5de3dc0f9d4466a1d06b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Some chapters require the GitHub CLI, GitHub repositories, and GitHub Actions; later sections involve local and remote MCP servers and running Claude Code within Cursor and the Claude desktop application."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1efa3524b52f3987b44568202341fb57f9bcc4690f043de7b8cefcdb6ad1a2a4","clm_3a837e59a0a02f7039969271bd8c31d0eef2232f07e867cba4304b03a513b78e","clm_3c667a14832daaa246808d3322d6c555f1f29f6ac9849d33169686cf98d84643","clm_58f61a5716b19a1cbaf02417f0dcb8862b576f7129b139aeaa90c9348cee7710","clm_774edcad2b1ed0593af3dcd5ce780b6ae055a3ff4f1e1640ef3098ae236838e0","clm_9d356b9b31b18c64cafdfdc905df00ca6882c22ad6f999a655f9d75793dbda82","clm_bf3223ed98b30224c316967a0253b04e660594afe9cdf786952b2b8e3c59c411","clm_fa977be76ec5f0fc2072538600fb0c53c104162583bd5de3dc0f9d4466a1d06b"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:15:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_94aab6edb291412fac6f87564f1c6c4e","id":"pg_e09f42e2321856b3880785dd2fc28fc6","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/packtpublishing-agentic-coding-with-claude-code-readme-md-78131f7a050f-85dd2fc28fc6.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_f0c0d8e1637e5768b8bbe95e19e2cc38"],"title":"PacktPublishing/Agentic-Coding-with-Claude-Code/README.md @ 78131f7a050f","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:15:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_94aab6edb291412fac6f87564f1c6c4e"}
